        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1524">

                <pb facs="0981" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/288.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Letcher.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[No. 298.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your dispatch
                    No. 524 of August 6, 1914, in regard to the estate of the late Mr. William S.
                    Benton.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to call the attention of General Villa to the fact that a
                    representative of the Benton estate has been continuously in charge of the
                    property and that the temporary tenants upon the property should be informed by
                    Villa that they are tenants of the Benton estate and must pay their rents to the
                    estate’s representative.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
